+**MIX files (1.34):** the MIX FILE row (a name, EXPORT, IMPORT, CROSSMIX 0-15 s) saves and loads `<name>.mdfm.json`, a small JSON file with every station's What plays switches, the instruments and the whole mix (not the skin or the volume). `radio.getSettings({name})` makes one; `radio.applySettings(file, {crossmix})` puts one on, gliding over `crossmix` seconds while on air (switches change halfway; a file from another station tunes there), and resolves `{name, station, crossmix, skipped}`. The `mixfile` event (`start`, `switch`, `done`) lets a page tick its own checkboxes (`skin/radio-wire.js` does). `exportMix(radio, {name, app})`, `readMixFile(file)` and `mixFileName(name)` are exported for pages with their own buttons. The format is described at the top of `src/mixfile.js`.
